Dump bud_aer_mas, the per-process mass-flux array, once per chemistry step.

ukca_aero_step fills 283 budget slots -- condensation by vapour and by mode,
nucleation, coagulation per mode pair, ageing, mode merging -- and the shipped
driver allocates the array, zeroes it every step, and never writes it out.

Exposing it is what turns validation from "the final number matches" into
"H2SO4 condensation onto the accumulation mode matches at step 7". Budgets alone
are not sufficient (they carry mass fluxes only, no nd/mdt/drydp) which is what
the state-snapshot overlay adds; but they localise every mass-transfer pathway.

Written AFTER the step and before the next step's reset, since budgets
accumulate over one chemistry step only. Slot 0 is emitted even though upstream
never writes it -- every write is IF (nmasxxx > 0) guarded -- so the column
index equals the Fortran budget index with no off-by-one, and a non-zero value
there is itself a finding.

Controlled by budget_file in &box_run; empty means not written, so existing
namelists are unaffected.

Applied to a staged copy at build time; fortran/ is never modified.
